WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.034
New allegations tonight that

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.068
there are recordings

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:02.736
and a lot of them

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:03.837
that should have been provided

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:05.205
in the Dominion Voting Systems

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:06.473
case against Fox.

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:06.806
That's what

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:07.674
Abby Grosberg

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:08.241
fired, Fox

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:08.942
senior producer

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:09.843
who once worked with Tucker

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:10.744
Carlson, who was fired

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:13.813
yesterday, is saying is saying a reminder

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:14.881
that Grossberg has filed

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:16.983
two lawsuits against Fox and says she was

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:18.151
let go for it.

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:18.885
She accuses

00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:19.686
Fox of promoting

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:20.887
a hostile work environment

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:21.721
with claims of rampant

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:23.056
sexism and misogyny

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:24.991
among Carlson's show team.

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:26.092
According to our reporting,

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.794
that may have been one of the reasons

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:29.996
why Carlson was fired yesterday.

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:31.064
Grossberg also claims

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:31.731
she was pressured

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:32.932
to give misleading comments

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:34.234
in the Dominion case.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:35.602
Today, she told MSNBC

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:36.269
Nicolle Wallace

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:37.137
she has many audio

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:38.438
recordings from her devices,

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:38.972
and she claims

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:41.041
Dominion said that they didn't have them

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:43.710
I have several

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.545
recordings that I'm still going through

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:46.413
that we've recovered

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:47.480
from all of the phones.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.316
There are 90 that we have

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:52.552
90 recordings

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:54.087
not long after that, her attorney

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:56.122
speaking on MSNBC said the Jack Smith,

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:56.856
the special counsel

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:58.625
on the January six investigation,

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:00.360
wants those recordings.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.361
A Fox spokesperson

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:02.062
has previously said

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:03.630
The Goldbergs lawsuits are, quote,

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.098
riddled with false allegations

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:07.300
against the network and her employees.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.668
I want to get perspective on this

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:10.003
and what it means for a broader news

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:11.704
media landscape without Tucker Carlson

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:13.506
and from media critic David Zurawik.

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:15.008
David, good to have you on.

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:15.608
Do you have a sense

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:18.978
of how much of a role of any Abby

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.080
Goldberg's allegations

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:21.047
may have played in Tucker

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:22.082
Carlson's ouster?

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:23.383
I mean, is it clear really why

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:24.350
he was fired at this point?

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:26.319
It isn't.

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:28.221
It isn't clear why he was fired.

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:30.323
And I think really

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:32.659
this story has such large cultural

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:36.763
reverberations for it

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.064
that we should be careful

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:39.365
and that we shouldn't say

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:41.000
this is why it happened.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.503
There's been so much of that

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:45.572
Anderson, in the last couple of days.

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:47.073
And purposely in the piece

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:49.742
I wrote for CNN, I pulled back from that.

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:51.945
But if you look at history,

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:53.913
there is some indication here

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:56.916
that this culture is still in place.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.285
The culture of sexism,

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:01.488
misogyny, really a culture

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:03.123
that debases women

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:06.793
was built into the DNA of Fox News

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:08.128
by Roger Ailes,

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:09.696
the the founder,

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:09.963
you know,

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:11.264
the master propagandist,

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:13.666
the political operative who founded this.

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:17.070
We saw it down the line in Bill O'Reilly.

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:20.740
Fox talked about as if they excised

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.976
this cancer when they got rid of Ailes

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:25.211
and O'Reilly. Bill O'Reilly, the host.

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:27.113
And that was really dramatic.

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:29.883
But even cutting off the head with Ailes

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:30.950
and then O'Reilly,

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:33.786
you don't change a culture overnight.

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:35.021
I wrote at the time that

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:35.522
this is like

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:36.356
a cancer

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:39.192
at the heart of Fox News internally

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:42.262
and they really have to make a series

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:46.399
systematic attempt to eradicate it.

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:47.400
I don't think

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.036
that they made that kind of attempt.

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:52.872
If her allegations are true, Anderson,

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:55.175
they didn't do much about it at all.

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:55.842
You covered

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:57.777
I mean, Tucker Carlson for many years.

00:02:57.777 --> 00:03:00.780
Is it clear to you how or even

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:04.784
why this his persona became what it did?

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:05.285
I mean, was

00:03:05.285 --> 00:03:07.220
he always in this for the money?

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:09.455
And he was just reading the tea

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:10.623
leaves of where the

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:11.024
you know,

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:12.325
and following the money to

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:14.894
to where he thought the audience was.

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:16.396
And it was

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:18.331
very financially lucrative for him

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:19.899
because I talked to Paul Begala

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:20.533
last night

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:21.367
to work with Carlson

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.802
on CROSSFIRE here on CNN.

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:24.871
And Paul basically said that back then,

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:25.171
you know,

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:26.673
Carlson was very contrarian,

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:27.707
didn't like to be managed,

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.676
but the Fox version of him

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:31.611
was not the person he knew way back then.

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:34.948
Well, you know, I think it's always hard

00:03:34.948 --> 00:03:36.349
to figure out whether someone

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:38.218
is manipulating the system

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:40.687
or being seduced and manipulated by it.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:43.723
I think that that wasn't always the way

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:44.524
Carlson was.

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:46.659
I would agree with Begala about that.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.561
But I think it was the man

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:49.562
meeting the moment

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.631
when he got that show at Fox.

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:55.068
We had the ascent of Donald Trump.

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:57.937
And I think he saw what Trump did,

00:03:57.971 --> 00:04:00.540
how Trump used transgressive behavior

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.242
to an outrage

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:03.610
to gather attention

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:05.812
to himself, to control the media.

00:04:05.812 --> 00:04:06.379
I mean,

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:07.080
you know,

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.048
I wrestled in a million columns with

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:10.383
how do we cover this guy?

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:10.683
You know,

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:11.884
we can't keep covering him

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:12.685
when he says things

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:13.920
we know that aren't true.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.488
All we can do is say it's not true.

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:16.623
But we never figured out

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:18.091
exactly how to cover him.

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:19.425
And just as Trump

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:20.793
did in the political realm,

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:21.494
by going

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:23.329
where no one else would go, saying

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:24.497
horrible things,

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:26.432
insulting people in horrible

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:28.568
ways, saying racist stuff.

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:30.570
Tucker Carlson did the same thing

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:33.106
in the media realm, like when he said

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:34.240
that immigrants

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:36.042
he suggested that immigrants

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:37.710
make us dirtier as a nation.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.112
That's a racist statement.

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:41.247
That's just outrageous.

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:42.749
I can't think of any mainstream

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:43.616
journalist

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:45.618
who would even want to think that,

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:46.586
let alone say.

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:47.520
But he said it.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.322
He gets enormous coverage.

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:50.390
His ratings

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:53.326
he he feeds the base of his far

00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:54.227
right further

00:04:54.227 --> 00:04:56.296
and further out their audience.

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:57.764
And it looks like he owns,

00:04:57.764 --> 00:04:59.232
quote, owns the libs.

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:00.333
And so they're delighted

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:02.335
the level of hypocrisy, though, of him,

00:05:02.335 --> 00:05:03.836
you know, saying he,

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:05.838
you know, things he hates Donald Trump.

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:06.506
He can't wait

00:05:06.506 --> 00:05:07.940
until he doesn't have to cover him.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:08.808
They're almost there.

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:10.143
They don't have to have him on, you know,

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:11.311
they don't have to talk about him

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:12.145
every night.

00:05:12.145 --> 00:05:12.845
I mean,

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:14.847
it's just so hypocritical

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:17.583
to be saying one thing privately and

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:19.485
saying something else on air.

00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:21.888
I mean, it just it's stunning.

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:25.024
And there's Anderson, to you and me

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:26.626
and intellectually,

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:26.993
people

00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:28.895
who try to be intellectually consistent

00:05:28.895 --> 00:05:32.165
and honest The hypocrisy makes you gag.

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:34.067
But I think in the world

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:36.736
he operated in somehow in his mind.

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:37.537
And I

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:39.138
you know, I don't again, I don't know.

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:40.473
But I think, you know, it's easy

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:42.175
to get seduced by the power.

00:05:42.175 --> 00:05:42.408
You know,

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:44.277
every time you go out there

00:05:44.277 --> 00:05:45.311
and say certain things,

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:46.979
you get great feedback, you know?

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:49.315
And I think he got caught up in that

00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:49.982
a little bit.

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:50.783
I think in some ways

00:05:50.783 --> 00:05:51.784
he got caught up in it

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:53.553
and hoisted on his own.

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:54.153
There's nothing

00:05:54.153 --> 00:05:55.054
there's no greater reminder

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:56.823
of how perilous one it is

00:05:56.823 --> 00:05:59.325
than being quickly fired and

00:05:59.325 --> 00:06:00.560
zipping off the screen

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:02.895
and then suddenly seeing how different

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:04.530
the world is. David Zurawik.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:05.531
Appreciate it. Thank you.

